.TH DANBY-PARASITE 1
.SH NAME
danby-parasite \- host-limited parasite population growth
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/parasite
.SH MODEL
H' = rH(1-H/K)-bHP;
P' = cbHP-dP.
.PP
Hosts H grow logistically.  Parasites P increase only through host contact and
conversion, while infection removes hosts.  The display therefore distinguishes
host carrying capacity from parasite carrying capacity induced by hosts.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the host or parasite state bar.  The five tracks set host growth and
capacity, infection, conversion, and parasite death.  Space pauses, period
steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/parasite.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/parasite.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR danby-epidemic (1)
